Hi,

 =


I ve send a message yesterday regarding Motorola modem H24 and static
config.

Today I ve achieved to create a plugin for this modem and make it
recognized by udev. I also succeed to perform a voice call :-)

 =


Now I want to set up a gprs connection, but it s quite hard to
understand how to setup a gprs connection.

I ve send following:

 =


dbus-send --system --type=3Dmethod_call --print-reply --dest=3Dorg.ofono
/h240 org.ofono.ConnectionManager.SetProperty string:"Powered"
variant:boolean:true

dbus-send --system --type=3Dmethod_call --print-reply --dest=3Dorg.ofono
/h240 org.ofono.ConnectionManager.SetProperty string:"RoamingAllowed"
variant:boolean:true

dbus-send --system --type=3Dmethod_call --print-reply --dest=3Dorg.ofono
/h240 org.ofono.ConnectionManager.AddContext string:"internet"

dbus-send --system --type=3Dmethod_call --print-reply --dest=3Dorg.ofono
/h240/context2 org.ofono.ConnectionContext.SetProperty string:"Active"
variant:boolean:true

 =


but here I get an unimplemented error.

 =


Can you give me some information on steps to do to setup a gprs
connection ?

 =


Today my plugin is quite simple (more or less a copy of  tc65.c). Are
you interesting by getting a patch containing this early support of h24
motorola modem ?

 =


BR

Christophe

